  {
   "t": 1793255409292,
   "text": "The Eiffel Tower is **330 metres (1,083 ft) tall**, measured to the tip of its antenna, according to its English Wikipedia article.\n\nOther heights the article gives:\n- **Without the antenna:** 300 m (984 ft)\n- **Top floor:** 276 m (906 ft)\n\nThe article says that's about the height of an 81-storey building, and it's the tallest structure in Paris. The tower was the tallest structure in the world from 1889 until the Chrysler Building was finished in 1930. A broadcasting antenna added in 1957 made it 11 m taller than the Chrysler Building."
  }
